So I tried Slash'EM for the first time today. Of course I went for
Doppleganger, who can pass up being able to polymorph into whatever
they want whenever? After a few deaths in the new levels I think I'm
doing pretty well...

I got to level 12 and I'm almost 13, with a potion of gain level for
when I make it. I'm on DLVL 18, walking around a Master Mind Flayer. I
find a portal and enter it.. There's another new kind of monster here,
a killer pile of coins. They have no brains so Mind Flayer isn't very
effective. So I step on the portal, and #youpoly into a Vampire Lord,
then re-enter and clear out the killer coins. In the next room is a
priest of Crom. Crom is my god, so this must be a co-aligned altar
room, right?

I have quite a bit of gold at this point so I figure I'll buy some
protection. #chat at Priest of Crom. The Priest of Crom says "So you
want to chat? Well this is what I have to say!" Then priest proceeded
to hit me with his mace, cast a spell which paralyzed me, kick me,
doing 70 damage  sending me back to Doopleganger form, then hits and
kicks me for my 100 natural hit points until I'm dead. Nice.

My gravestone says I died while on the Lawful quest, although I was
neutral. Why was there a priest of Crom in the lawful quest? I figured
that whatever alignment you are means only that quest exists for you in
the game, but I'm guessing all three quests exist? And why did he go
beserk on me... was he mad that I was polymorphed into a Vamp Lord?
Must be some other new thing in Slash'EM that I don't know about. Looks
like it's time to start over again...



